WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.001 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-How are you?

00:00:01.001 --> 00:00:02.635 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm just having
a relaxing bath.

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:04.471 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's it.
-Yeah, this film is about

00:00:04.471 --> 00:00:07.107 align:start size:94% position:6%
a relaxing bath.
-It's just a cozy night in.

00:00:07.107 --> 00:00:12.012
-This was a terrifying movie
for me to watch because --

00:00:12.012 --> 00:00:15.081
Well, I guess we should explain
what's happening there.

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:16.683 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is your --
-I'm in labor.

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:18.918
-You're in labor.
-I'm not having a relaxing bath.

00:00:18.918 --> 00:00:21.454
-Yeah, you're in labor.
-Attempting to give birth

00:00:21.454 --> 00:00:22.956 align:start size:94% position:6%
silently.
-And you are giving birth

00:00:22.956 --> 00:00:25.759
silently because the monsters
in this film are attracted

00:00:25.759 --> 00:00:27.861 align:start size:94% position:6%
to sound.
-Yes, like acutely attracted.

00:00:27.861 --> 00:00:32.332
-And my wife's about to have a
baby, and it was not a good time

00:00:32.332 --> 00:00:34.034 align:start size:94% position:6%
to watch this movie.
-Listen, I did it silently.

00:00:34.034 --> 00:00:35.902 align:start size:94% position:6%
She can do it.
-[ Laughing ] She can do it.

00:00:35.902 --> 00:00:38.271 align:start size:94% position:6%
Although I guess the upside is
no matter how it goes,

00:00:38.271 --> 00:00:41.174
at least there won't be a sound
monster in the delivery room.

00:00:41.174 --> 00:00:43.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Apart from you screaming.
-That's true.

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:45.979 align:start size:94% position:6%
Which I did last time,
to a great effect.

00:00:45.979 --> 00:00:48.181 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, you did? Yeah.
-So, this is the first time

00:00:48.181 --> 00:00:49.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
you and John
have worked together.

00:00:49.983 --> 00:00:51.985
-Yeah!
-I'm assuming people have tried

00:00:51.985 --> 00:00:53.520 align:start size:94% position:6%
to get you to do things
in the past.

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:55.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, they have,
but we've sort of been offered

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:56.923 align:start size:94% position:6%
every romantic comedy
under the sun.

00:00:56.923 --> 00:01:00.126
But no one wants to see John
and I kind of meeting in a film.

00:01:00.126 --> 00:01:03.530
Like, people wouldn't buy it.
Like, "Hey, I'm Meredith,"

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:06.366 align:start size:94% position:6%
and like, "Hey, I'm Paul."
You know, it's like --

00:01:06.366 --> 00:01:08.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's never good.
-Yeah, that's true.

00:01:08.368 --> 00:01:10.203
-'Cause that's how
all romantic comedies go, guys.

00:01:10.203 --> 00:01:12.839
-Usually, there's always a Paul.
-There's, like, a template.

00:01:12.839 --> 00:01:16.609 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
But this horror film,

00:01:16.609 --> 00:01:18.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
he directed, he co-wrote it.
-Yeah.

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:19.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And --
-He's a show-off.

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:21.714
-He's a show-off, he really is.
And he's wonderful in it.

00:01:21.714 --> 00:01:24.284 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Indistinct ]
-Was this a case of him trying

00:01:24.284 --> 00:01:27.153
to get you to do it, you trying
to get him to put you in it,

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:28.822 align:start size:94% position:6%
or did you immediately
both agree to it?

00:01:28.822 --> 00:01:31.124 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, we've always
sort of been protective of

00:01:31.124 --> 00:01:34.094 align:start size:94% position:6%
each other's projects.
And in this case,

00:01:34.094 --> 00:01:36.729
he got sent the script and I had
just had our second child,

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:39.999 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, literally just had
our second child -- silently.

00:01:39.999 --> 00:01:41.234 align:start size:94% position:6%
And --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:42.669 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was about
to do Mary Poppins,

00:01:42.669 --> 00:01:44.904 size:84% position:42%
so I wasn't in the sort
of headspace of, like,

00:01:44.904 --> 00:01:48.475 size:81% position:41%
horrific horror movie.
But then he wrote it,

00:01:48.475 --> 00:01:50.777 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then I read it
and I just loved it.

00:01:50.777 --> 00:01:52.946 align:start size:94% position:6%
So this was the one.
I just thought the concept was

00:01:52.946 --> 00:01:56.483
so ambitious, so unique.
It was sort of bigger than

00:01:56.483 --> 00:01:58.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
the fact that we were
a married couple in a movie

00:01:58.585 --> 00:02:01.354 align:start size:94% position:6%
together, you know.
-It's incredibly

00:02:01.354 --> 00:02:02.155 align:start size:94% position:6%
tightly plotted.
-Yeah.

00:02:02.155 --> 00:02:04.624 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's a really efficient film
in that there's

00:02:04.624 --> 00:02:06.359 align:start size:94% position:6%
this really great premise
and I feel like

00:02:06.359 --> 00:02:08.027 align:start size:94% position:6%
it played out beautifully.
-Thank you.

00:02:08.027 --> 00:02:11.564 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And terrifyingly.
I feel like it's so beautiful.

00:02:11.564 --> 00:02:12.532 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.532 --> 00:02:17.337 align:start size:94% position:6%
But once you decided to do it,
was he all-in on the idea?

00:02:17.337 --> 00:02:20.707 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, he was so excited.
And I was awkward about it.

00:02:20.707 --> 00:02:22.675
I was like, "Would you ever want
me to do this movie,

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:24.344 size:84% position:42%
or would that be weird?
I mean, you don't have

00:02:24.344 --> 00:02:27.413
to say yes, I don't know."
And he was really happy.

00:02:27.413 --> 00:02:31.217
-Now, obviously he spent a lot
of time working on the script,

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:33.486 align:start size:94% position:6%
co-writing it.
Are you a good person

00:02:33.486 --> 00:02:35.889 align:start size:94% position:6%
to bounce ideas off?
-I mean, I thought I was.

00:02:35.889 --> 00:02:39.359
And then he informed me that I
had, like, a resting bitchface.

00:02:39.359 --> 00:02:42.228
I wasn't aware that was a thing.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:44.497 size:84% position:42%
I understand there's
a hashtag or something.

00:02:44.497 --> 00:02:48.535
But yeah, I had heard it
from a couple of directors

00:02:48.535 --> 00:02:52.372
that I'm very impassive
when you're pitching me an idea.

00:02:52.372 --> 00:02:56.376 align:start size:94% position:6%
And his impersonation of me is
when he's enthusiastically

00:02:56.376 --> 00:02:59.212 align:start size:94% position:6%
pitching me an idea,
that I just go like this.

00:02:59.212 --> 00:03:01.181 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:01.181 --> 00:03:06.085
And not strangely quickly. Like,
sort of crunching the numbers

00:03:06.085 --> 00:03:07.620 align:start size:94% position:6%
on whether I liked it or not.
-I shouldn't say

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:10.456
that is not an accurate reaction
to a single thing that happens

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:12.392 align:start size:94% position:6%
in this film.
There's not a single scare

00:03:12.392 --> 00:03:15.328
where you're like, "Uh-huh."
-Like, "Okay, whatever," yeah.

00:03:15.328 --> 00:03:18.698 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And then, is it weird --
I would imagine for

00:03:18.698 --> 00:03:20.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
the birthing scene...
-Yeah.

00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:22.502
-...like it must be very hard
for the man who is in the room

00:03:22.502 --> 00:03:25.004
when you actually gave two
children to give you direction.

00:03:25.004 --> 00:03:27.140 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Gave two children to him.
-Yeah. [ Laughs ]

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:29.909
Does he just sort of let
you use your own instincts?

00:03:29.909 --> 00:03:32.612
-Honestly, I think if he'd had
one note I would've been like,

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:35.215 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Shut up," right?
"You don't know."

00:03:35.215 --> 00:03:39.686
So yeah, he kind of just let me
have a freewheeling experience

00:03:39.686 --> 00:03:41.087 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
during that time.

